I'm preparing for an Applied AI/ML Senior Engineer interview, with a focus on machine learning system design metric choosing.

Here are some metrics for each category

MSE (Mean Squared Error)
MAE (Mean Absolute Error)
Huber Loss
Notes: Smooth transition between MSE and MAE.
Quantile Loss
Notes: Corrected to standard pinball-loss convention (original had lambda
       inverted).
RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)
Notes: Square root of MSE.
Asymmetric Huber Loss
Notes: No single standard form -- typically Huber with asymmetric delta
       (delta+ for positive errors, delta- for negative).
Log-Cosh Loss (supplemental)
Notes: Common smooth alternative to Huber; ~= 1/2*x^2 near 0,
       ~= |x| - log 2 for large errors.
Classification Losses and Metrics
Cross Entropy / Log Loss
Notes: Binary cross-entropy.
Normalized Cross Entropy (NCE)
Notes: Normalizes model logloss by the entropy of the base rate.
Focal Loss
Notes: Canonical form (Lin et al. 2017) includes alpha:
       -alpha_t*(1-p_t)^gamma * log(p_t).
Hinge Loss
Notes: Standard form -- supplemental addition.
KL Divergence (supplemental)
Notes: Common for distribution-matching tasks.
Forecast Metrics
MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error)
Notes: Divide-by-zero risk when A_t = 0.
SMAPE (Symmetric Mean Absolute Percentage Error)
Notes: Bounded to [0%, 200%].
MASE (supplemental)
Notes: Scale-independent; avoids MAPE's divide-by-zero issue;
       <1 beats naive forecast.
WAPE (supplemental)
Notes: Common in demand forecasting; weighted/relative version of MAE.
Ranking Metrics
NDCG (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain)
Notes: Measures ranking quality with position discount; IDCG is DCG of
       ideal ordering.
MAP (Mean Average Precision)
Notes: Average of average precision across queries; m = relevant items,
       P(k) = precision at cutoff k.
MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank)
Notes: rank_q = position of first relevant result for query q.
Precision@K
Notes: Simple top-K precision; ignores order within K.
Recall@K
Notes: Fraction of relevant items retrieved in top K.
Pairwise Hinge (Ranking SVM)
Notes: Enforces margin between positive (x+) and negative (x-) item scores.
F1@K
Notes: Harmonic mean of precision and recall at cutoff K.
LambdaRank
Notes: Gradient-based ranker that optimizes NDCG directly via a weighted
       pairwise gradient.
RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Metrics
Recall@K (retrieval): Reused from Ranking. Did relevant chunk(s) appear in top K retrieved.
Precision@K (retrieval): Reused from Ranking. Fraction of retrieved chunks that are relevant.
Hit Rate@K: Binary version of recall@K. At least one relevant chunk in top K.
MRR / NDCG (retrieval ordering): Reused from Ranking. Matters when chunk order affects truncation or context weighting.
Context Precision: Fraction of retrieved chunks that are actually relevant. Penalizes noisy context that dilutes the LLM's window.
Context Relevance: Whether retrieved context relates to the query at all. Inverse framing of Context Precision.
Faithfulness / Groundedness: Does the generated answer only assert what's supported by retrieved context. Typically LLM-judged (entailment scoring). Core hallucination metric for RAG.
Answer Relevance: Does the generated answer actually address the question. Distinct from whether it's grounded.
BLEU / ROUGE / BERTScore (supplemental): Reference-based NLG overlap metrics. Weak fit for open-ended RAG QA since there's rarely one correct phrasing. Mention as context, explain limitation.
RAGAS (framework note): Common framework bundling Faithfulness, Answer Relevance, Context Precision/Relevance into one eval suite.
Chatbot / Conversational Metrics
Task Success Rate / Task Completion Rate: Did the conversation resolve the user's actual goal. North-star metric for assistant-style bots.
Intent Classification Accuracy / F1: Standard classification metrics for the NLU/routing layer. Precision/recall/F1 per intent, confusion matrix for commonly confused intents.
Slot-Filling Accuracy: Correctness of structured field extraction (dates, amounts, destinations) within a turn.
Containment Rate / Deflection Rate: Fraction of conversations resolved without human escalation.
Escalation Rate: Inverse-ish signal. Watch timing. Late escalation wastes turns. Early escalation may signal good self-awareness by the bot.
Turns-to-Resolution: Efficiency measure. Too high suggests confusion loops. Too low may mean premature/wrong closure.
Coherence: Whether the bot maintains context and avoids self-contradiction across turns. Typically LLM-judged.
Repetition / Loop Rate: Bot re-asking or repeating itself. Common production failure mode.
Fallback Rate: Frequency of "I don't understand" or default responses.
Hallucination Rate: Ties back to Faithfulness in RAG section.
Toxicity / Policy-Violation Rate: Safety metric. Frequency of harmful or policy-violating outputs.
Refusal Rate / Over-Refusal Rate: Trade-off metric. Too-cautious bots hurt task completion.
Business / Online Metrics (cross-cutting, supplemental)
CSAT / Thumbs Up-Down Rate / NPS: Direct user satisfaction signal. Applicable to RAG and chatbot products.
Handle Time Reduction: Vs. human-only baseline. Key for enterprise/support chatbots.
Retention / Repeat Usage: Of the chatbot channel specifically.
Cost per Resolved Conversation: Compute cost at scale. Often overlooked in offline-metric-only discussions.

